      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T20:04:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or you can add a callback in thermal_command_get_threshold:\n\n    if (board_get_fan_custom(p-\u003esensor_num))\n        return EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE;\n\nThen, get_thermal_fan_percent can return rv (instead of -1):\n\n    if (rv \u003c\u003d 0)\n        return -1;\n\nand cmd_temperature_print should check:\n\n    if (rv \u003d\u003d -EECRESULT - EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE)\n        printf(\"n/a\");\n\nI think it should work but please try.\n\n--- \u003e8 ---\n\nWhat would be a much better solution is to add a new command, which returns an actual fan speed in % or in RPM. For custom fans, board_get_fan_speed(int fan) should return RPM or %. Then, we get rid of EC_CMD_THERMAL_GET_THRESHOLD from get_thermal_fan_percent, which is currently duplicating the computation done by the EC (\u003d\u003d thermal_fan_percent).",
      "parentUuid": "5dd830e9_8bc72a5a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3278,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3280,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "2cbd209b6603e5568f030dbe74eb6d1994ab9c81",
